       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision. OTC use tops out at 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day divided differently**, for example 600 mg or 400 mg at some other frequency\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with your rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
